1. PURPOSE
Stack 53.0 defines the executable implementation architecture required to connect the OneDraft platform to authorized ArcGIS repositories and services.
Stack 52.0 established the Global Geospatial Application, Repository & World-Model architecture.
Stack 53.0 converts that architecture into an implementation specification governing:
ArcGIS connectivity
Repository integration
GIS dataset registration
Spatial data ingestion
Spatial data normalization
Feature and layer management
Coordinate-reference management
Spatial synchronization
Project georeferencing
Authorized repository write-back
Spatial provenance
Version management
Conflict management
API integration
Job execution
Database persistence
Security
Testing
Deployment
The objective is to establish a concrete implementation boundary between the OneDraft application and external ArcGIS infrastructure while preserving OneDraft as an independent architectural and engineering platform.

2. IMPLEMENTATION OBJECTIVE
The objective of Stack 53.0 is to provide the executable system required to establish:
ONEDRAFT
   ↓
GEOSPATIAL APPLICATION
   ↓
ARCGIS ADAPTER
   ↓
ARCGIS SERVICES
   ↓
ARCGIS REPOSITORY
and the reverse information path:
ARCGIS REPOSITORY
   ↓
ARCGIS ADAPTER
   ↓
INGESTION
   ↓
NORMALIZATION
   ↓
VALIDATION
   ↓
ONEDRAFT SPATIAL MODEL
   ↓
PROJECT / SITE / STRUCTURE
The implementation shall support controlled bidirectional interaction without collapsing the distinction between external GIS information and canonical OneDraft project information.

3. IMPLEMENTATION PRINCIPLE
The primary implementation principle shall be:
ARCGIS
PROVIDES EXTERNAL GEOSPATIAL DATA
        ↓
ONEDRAFT
